@namespace Shiny.Blazor.Controls

@*
    A row of items inside a group — the other way to fill one, and the one a run of formatting marks
    wants.

    A group's items normally fill a column top to bottom and start the next when it is full. That is
    right for a set of interchangeable commands and wrong for a run: bold, italic, underline and
    strikethrough are read left to right, and a two-row column turns four of them into a 2x2 block with
    underline above italic. It also forces a font-name box and a bold button into one column, where
    `min-content` sizes the column to the box and `justify-items: stretch` draws the 16px B across all
    150px of it.

    Put rows in a group and the group lays them out as rows instead. The group needs no mode set: the
    stylesheet switches on :has(.shiny-ribbon-row), so the presence of a row IS the signal.
*@
<div class="shiny-ribbon-row" role="group">
    @this.ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
